Dashora Organizer Source-Available License 1.2

1. Scope

This license applies to the original Dashora Organizer code and other materials
expressly distributed under this license (the "Software"). "Licensors" means
the copyright holders offering those materials under this license.

The "Official Repository" is https://github.com/mohaidr/focus-board.
"Authorized Maintainers" means maintainers authorized by the applicable
Licensors to review and merge contributions into the Official Repository.

The "Software" includes the application as accessed through a hosted service,
not only downloaded or self-hosted copies.

For this license, "Commercial Use" means use for or within a for-profit business,
or use in providing paid services or pursuing commercial advantage. It includes
internal business use, use by employees or contractors for business work, and
commercial hosting, even if no fee is charged for access to Dashora itself.
Personal use unrelated to business and noncommercial educational, charitable,
or public-institution use are not Commercial Use.

Third-party components, libraries, fonts, and other materials remain governed
by their own licenses. This license does not replace or restrict those licenses.
It does not apply to content you create or store using the Software.

2. Permitted use

Subject to the conditions below, the Licensors grant you a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free license to:

(a) Run and use the Software for lawful noncommercial purposes.
(b) Copy, install, and self-host unmodified versions of the Software, including
    hosting an unmodified version for others' noncommercial use.
(c) Redistribute unmodified copies of the Software with this license and all
    existing copyright, attribution, and third-party notices intact, for
    noncommercial purposes.
(d) Modify the Software solely for your own personal use or your organization's
    internal use, provided the modified version remains a version of Dashora
    Organizer and complies with Section 3. Commercial Use of either an
    unmodified or privately modified version also requires qualification
    under Section 4.
(e) Publish proposed modifications solely for contribution review through the
    Official Repository's public pull-request process, including a public fork
    or branch necessary for that process, subject to Section 4. This exception
    does not permit distributing a separate modified product or hosting it for
    public use.

No license fee is required for these permitted activities.
Commercial Use is permitted without a license fee upon qualification under
Section 4, with no separate commercial approval required.

3. Restrictions

Without separate written permission from the applicable Licensors, you may not:

(a) Copy, extract, incorporate, port, or otherwise reuse any of the Software's
    code in another application, product, library, or codebase, whether that
    other project is commercial or noncommercial, public or private.
(b) Distribute, publish, sublicense, or otherwise provide modified versions
    of the Software, including modified source code, to third parties,
    except through the contribution-review process in Section 2(e).
(c) Host or otherwise make a modified version available for use outside your
    own personal use or your organization's internal use.
(d) Remove or misrepresent the Software's copyright, attribution, or license
    notices.

Commercial Use requires qualification under Section 4. A public push or an
unmerged pull request does not qualify; a qualifying feature merged by
Authorized Maintainers grants commercial permission automatically.

Copying the Software to deploy Dashora Organizer or to make the private
modifications permitted by Section 2 is not prohibited code reuse under
Section 3(a). Private modification does not authorize extracting or incorporating
the code into another application.

These restrictions apply only to rights controlled by the Licensors. They do
not restrict independently written code, general ideas, third-party materials
under their own licenses, or rights that applicable law does not allow this
license to restrict.

4. Contribution-based commercial permission

4.1 Qualifying feature

To qualify, an individual must author and publicly submit at least one complete
new feature through the Official Repository's contribution process. The feature
must be merged into the Official Repository by Authorized Maintainers.
Commercial permission begins automatically when that qualifying feature is
merged. No separate application, written approval, or commercial authorization
is required.

A qualifying feature must:

(a) Add a substantive new end-user capability with practical benefit to users
    beyond merely obtaining commercial permission.
(b) Be complete and usable in the application, not a placeholder, demonstration,
    disabled stub, or artificial splitting of a trivial change.
(c) Meet the project's applicable quality requirements, including documentation
    and tests appropriate to the feature.
(d) Be lawfully contributed by someone with authority to grant the rights
    described in Section 4.4.

Cosmetic changes, renaming, formatting, dependency updates, documentation-only
changes, and bug fixes alone do not satisfy the new-feature requirement.
Such contributions may still be welcome, but do not by themselves qualify.

Authorized Maintainers assess usefulness, completion, and quality during normal
contribution review. Merging a genuinely useful, complete new feature records
its acceptance for this license; no further eligibility review is required.
Features need not be large to qualify. Seeking commercial permission is a
welcome reason to contribute and does not disqualify a useful feature.
Submitting work does not guarantee that it will be merged.

4.2 Automatic permission and beneficiaries

The qualifying individual may exercise the Section 2 permissions for Commercial
Use without a license fee from the time of the qualifying merge. The public
merged pull request or commit identifying the contributor and feature is the
record of qualification.

The contributor may also extend this permission to one legal organization by
identifying that organization in the qualifying pull request or a public
comment on it. This designation requires no maintainer approval and takes
effect once both the qualifying merge and the designation have occurred.
It does not delay the individual's permission. At most one organization may
be designated, and that designation is nontransferable.

Permission is nontransferable and does not automatically cover an employer,
affiliate, subsidiary, client, successor, or other organization. Other users
of a hosted copy still need their own qualification for their Commercial Use.
No beneficiary may sublicense commercial eligibility.

Commercial permission does not permit code reuse in other applications,
redistribution of modified versions, or public hosting of modified versions.
All other restrictions continue to apply.

4.3 Misrepresentation and continuing conditions

Knowingly false authorship claims or other material misrepresentation used to
claim qualification grant no commercial permission. A placeholder or token
change that adds no genuine new capability does not qualify merely because
it was merged. These conditions do not disqualify a good-faith, useful feature
simply because its author wanted commercial permission.

Once validly earned, permission is not lost merely because the feature is later
changed, replaced, or removed, or because maintainers later change their opinion
of its usefulness. Permission remains subject to compliance with this license.
It covers
Software offered under this version of the license and does not promise rights
to future releases offered under different terms.

